1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Nenjukku Neethi. The autobiography of Kalaignar M. Karunanidhi.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,500
Volume One. Chapter One — "The Year of Birth."

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:16,000
The year, 1924. The village, Thirukkuvalai.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,000
How does an autobiography begin? With a question.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,000
"Have you become so great a man
as to write the story of your life?"

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
It was no one else who asked — his own heart asked it of him.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
And the heart held the answer too.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:46,000
"Do life and history belong only to the great?
Are they denied to the small?"

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Every person has a life-story;
history is not the property of the great alone.

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Only after granting his heart that verdict
did his pen begin, without hesitation.

11
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,000
He recalls the year of his birth with pride — 1924.

12
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:19,000
The First World War had ended; the great powers lay exhausted.

13
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Across the colonies, subject peoples were rising against their bondage.

14
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:33,000
That same year, Gandhi walked free from prison, on grounds of health;

15
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:41,000
and 1924 was the one year he officially presided over the Congress.

16
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:49,000
At the other end of the world, the revolutionary Lenin died that year —

17
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,000
one epoch closing, another opening.

18
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:02,000
In the Tamil country, the feeling for self-respect
and social justice was taking root.

19
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:08,000
And his teacher, Arignar Anna, was then a schoolboy.

20
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:20,000
"No year of the twentieth century," he writes,
"stood as great a question-mark as 1924."

21
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:36,000
That year, too, the fifty-year Cauvery water agreement
was made between Mysore and our state.

22
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Who could know that the child born in the year of that accord
would one day, as Chief Minister, speak for the same Cauvery?

23
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:53,000
"Even those who bore me would have called me 'Raja' —
would they ever have called me 'Minister'?"

24
00:02:53,000 --> 00:03:02,000
His village — in Thanjavur district, fifteen miles
from Thiruvarur — was Thirukkuvalai.

25
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:14,000
"A lovely temple-tank; a grove around it; the Shiva temple facing it."
That was the Thirukkuvalai he knew.

26
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:26,000
How a single life is woven into the history, society,
language and politics of its age —

27
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:32,000
this chapter tells quietly.

28
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:45,000
"The Year of Birth." Read the full chapter
in the original Tamil at nenjukkuneethi.org
